  <div class="faq"><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q"><span>What's the difference between cash credit and overdraft?</span><svg class="plus" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></button><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Both let you draw up to a sanctioned limit. CC is typically tied to current assets (stocks and receivables) with drawing power calculated monthly. OD can be unsecured or against other security (FD, property) with a fixed limit. The right structure depends on your business pattern.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q"><span>Will I need collateral for working capital?</span><svg class="plus" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></button><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">For larger limits, yes — usually primary security (inventory and receivables) plus collateral (property or FD). For smaller limits to established businesses, unsecured digital options exist.</div></div></div></div>
